error[type.unknown]: `i64` is a machine WIDTH, and widths live on an `extern fn`'s seats — this is not one
  ╭─[<case>/src/main.av:1:1]
1 │ fn n() -> i64 { 3 }
  · ┬
  · ╰── written here
──╯
help: Avra keeps one integer: write `int`. The widths (`i32`, `u32`, `i64`, `f64`) name what a C prototype declares, directly on an `extern fn`'s parameter or answer — never inside `List<…>`, and never on a value.
